# s99z — test stage exercising every editor feature.
#
# Layout: 100×100 OBJ units (10000×10000 PSX units at scale=100). One
# big floor + four perimeter walls. The visual mesh and collision mesh
# share their geometry — the visual side has only floor + walls; the
# collision side adds named trap_* and cam_* trigger volumes.
#
# UVs are square on every face so the same s99z.png tiles cleanly.
# Authored by hand (no Blender) so vertex order is human-readable.

mtllib s99z.mtl

# --- 4 floor corners + 4 wall-top corners (8 verts total) -----------
# Floor at Y=0, walls extruded up to Y=30 (= 3000 PSX units, snake-height).
v -50  0 -50
v  50  0 -50
v  50  0  50
v -50  0  50
v -50 30 -50
v  50 30 -50
v  50 30  50
v -50 30  50

# Square UV on every face (matches a 256×256 tile).
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0 1

usemtl s99z

o floor
f 1/1 2/2 3/3 4/4

# Walls: each is a vertical quad, two bottom verts on the floor + two
# top verts at Y=30. CCW from outside-the-room.
o wall_south
f 1/1 5/4 6/3 2/2
o wall_east
f 2/1 6/4 7/3 3/2
o wall_north
f 3/1 7/4 8/3 4/2
o wall_west
f 4/1 8/4 5/3 1/2
